From 58bb2581fd306cb8f53dac7a7aaf21ca5759d004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:54:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] serial: stm32: fix wakeup irq disabled when entering into
 low-power

If we spams the UART Rx during a suspend sequence, it may happen that the
platform goes into low-power mode without the RXNE enabled.

This happens because the interrupt routine could be called after the
suspend routine. The interrupt routine will disabled the RXNE interrupt to
avoid an irq storm, but the suspend is not stopped.

Change to pm_wakeup_hard_event() that will stop the suspend in this case.

Fixes: 368473ee8492 ("serial: stm32: replace wake up interrupt by rx not empty interrupt")
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Suggested-by: Kunliang YAO <kunliang.yao@st.com>
Change-Id: I8b4581b58a5b2340ecdb4ab59e737badb4c9249c
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/587501
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Christophe GUIBOUT <christophe.guibout@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
index dcd3d24bdfe4..6992cfc4fcde 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
@@ -1089,7 +1089,7 @@ static irqreturn_t stm32_usart_interrupt(int irq, void *ptr)
 		if (stm32_port->clk_am)
 			stm32_usart_disable_am(stm32_port);
 
-		pm_wakeup_event(tport->tty->dev, 0);
+		pm_wakeup_hard_event(tport->tty->dev);
 
 		ret = IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
-- 
2.53.0

